## Active quantified obligation

For each fixed M>=3 and sufficiently small positive wall curvature, exclude an arbitrary triangle-free old interior cloud of `N-1=3M^2-3M` sites in the six-direction curved unit-contact wall, or build an exact same-cardinality contact/diameter improvement. Then transfer to arbitrary macroscopic inactive containers, reconcile paired exterior caps, and close the independent full-core finite-move branch.

## Implication chains and status

1. One-deficit structural theorem -> controlled removable source guard / exact packet -> audit.64 full-source lexicographic contradiction. The arbitrary cloud is not presumed to be a lattice minus one site.
2. A strict N-site packet clearing all retained wall vertices after one deletion -> replaces all N-1 interior labels plus that corner -> contact loss. The inherited strict packet has only N-1 sites and cannot pay this count.
3. Exact-contact packet -> count every inserted-involving unit pair and verify triangle-freeness -> audit.64 if new contacts do not exceed removed contacts, strictly if no actual diameter is removed.

Dependencies presently needed: C-ONE-VERTEX-CONVEX-WALL-SHIELD, C-CONTACT-BUDGET-DIAMETER-EXCHANGE-ENDPOINT, C-NESTED-HEXAGON-STRESS-ENERGY-DEMAND; exact finite Oler inequality. Worker-1 checkpoints 14/15 are unreviewed leads. No canonical status is edited.

## Initial attacks

- Inspect one-point Oler slack using the finite triangulation proof rather than importing an equality conclusion.
- Search deliberate contact-budget packets and exact positive-stress blockers.
- Test whether the proposed all-cloud vacancy classification is stronger than known finite stability/solidity statements; if so replace it by a weaker triangle-forcing/exchange theorem.

No new theorem is asserted at this initial checkpoint. The goal remains active.

