The actual two-hop blocker graph Gamma forces equal signs whenever the
other endpoints of two incident unit edges are at distance >=sqrt(3):
opposite signs create a lower violation or unit triangle. Degree-five
vertices fuse all incident signs; degree-four vertices fuse opposite
pairs. A convex terminal face with nonconstant feasible signs must have
exactly four transitions at corners turning >pi/3, and those four actual
source vertices must form an inscribed parallelogram. Otherwise every
face boundary sign is equal. This is a finite coupled state restriction,
not an independent-owner model or infinitesimal-rhombus immunity claim.

Complete exact sign enumeration checks the regular hexagon (10/64 closed
